\title{One six-cycle, then a general factor}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The six-cycle of \ref{fdip-0057} has diagonal #{3} and neighbor
value #{1}. Integrating out its three odd vertices leaves a
triangle. The retained matrix has diagonal #{7/3} and
off-diagonal entries #{-1/3}. The same removal on a longer cycle,
or with more than one vertex between the vertices that remain,
is the calculation below.}
